From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:16:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] GSAttributedString: hash cached attribute dictionaries by
 content

The cache of attribute dictionaries used NSDictionary's -hash, which is
the dictionary's count, so every dictionary with the same number of keys
fell into one bucket and each lookup compared against all of them. Text
with many distinct attribute dictionaries (a heading anchor, link or
attachment each makes one) became quadratic to build: a 1.3 MB Markdown
document took 4.0s to render in MarkdownViewer, 1.2s with this change
(danjboyd/ObjcMarkdown#94).

The hash now adds each key's hash combined with its value's. Equal
dictionaries hash alike, as -isEqual: requires. A value whose hash
changes while it is cached (a mutated paragraph style) leaves its entry
unfound on removal: a leak, not a crash.

Carried in ObjcMarkdown's Linux packages; not sent upstream.
AI assistance: this change and this description were written with
Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code).
---
 Source/GSAttributedString.m | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/GSAttributedString.m b/Source/GSAttributedString.m
index 8fc9e60..a64d11c 100644
--- a/Source/GSAttributedString.m
+++ b/Source/GSAttributedString.m
@@ -117,6 +117,20 @@ cacheEqual(id A, id B)
 #define	GSI_MAP_RELEASE_KEY(M, X)	
 #define	GSI_MAP_RETAIN_VAL(M, X)	
 #define	GSI_MAP_RELEASE_VAL(M, X)	
+static inline NSUInteger
+cacheHash(NSDictionary *A)
+{
+  NSUInteger	h = [A count];
+  NSEnumerator	*e = [A keyEnumerator];
+  id		k;
+
+  while ((k = [e nextObject]) != nil)
+    {
+      h += [k hash] ^ [[A objectForKey: k] hash];
+    }
+  return h;
+}
+#define	GSI_MAP_HASH(M, X)	cacheHash((X).obj)
 #define	GSI_MAP_EQUAL(M, X,Y)	cacheEqual((X).obj, (Y).obj)
 #define GSI_MAP_KTYPES	GSUNION_OBJ
 #define GSI_MAP_VTYPES	GSUNION_NSINT
